# Helix HIG

The full guidelines live in `docs/design/helix-hig.md`. Read it before changing how anything looks; when a rule there is wrong, change the doc in the same piece of work.

Short version:

- GTK4/libadwaita defines the shared controls and styling constraints. Every surface is one tier: **Chrome** (panels, sidebars, headers, menus; glass per `transparency_mode`), **Leftover** (solid content: `applySectionCardStyle` / `applyContentCardStyle` / `applyGroupedListStyle`), **Modules** (`applyModuleWellStyle` solid controls), **Widgets** (glanceable, deep-link). Never glass-on-glass.
- One accent: `Primary` for selection, checked, progress, focus. `Hover` is a state (surface tinted toward the accent, derived in `src/ui/palette.cpp`), not a hue; hover borders use `Primary`. Secondary/tertiary are for meaning (charts, badges, status), never interaction.
- Roles, `Style::radius*`, `Style::space*`, `Style::fontSize*`, `Style::anim*` only; no literal colors or sizes. Control Center content and groups use `radiusXl`, solid fills, and no module softness.
- One compact card per tab; the header carries the title. Well and group headers are Body bold; `fontSizeTitle` is for values.
- Sibling repos (helix-niri, helix-greeter) change together when a shared contract changes; read their `HELIX.md` first.

```cpp
// BAD: leftover catalog as a second glass card on the glass panel
applySectionCardStyle(host, scale, opacity);

// GOOD: leftover catalog as grouped content on chrome
applyContentCardStyle(host, scale);
```
